WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:03.149
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:10.319
You have a rectangle with dimensions of 2 and 1 and you have a second rectangle of the same dimensions

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:19.198
Now rotate the second rectangle and place it on top of the first rectangle in such a way that they're opposite corners overlap

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:25.109
The question is what is the area of the overlapping region between the two rectangles?

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:28.019
I thank Robin for the suggestion

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:34.860
Pause the video, if you'd like to give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.619
I will present one way to solve this problem

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.350
Consider the following right triangle and suppose the other leg has a length equal to x

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:02.529
Since the entire side of the rectangle has a length equal to 2 the remaining length on this

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.779
Rectangle will be equal to 2 minus X

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.350
by symmetry

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.379
The other rectangle will have exactly the same lengths the portion that's not

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:17.229
overlapping will be equal to x and the portion that is overlapping will have a length equal to 2 - x

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.110
We can then consider just this right triangle

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.660
By the Gougu Theorem x squared plus 1 squared is equal to the quantity [2 - x] squared

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:32.379
We're going to expand the binomial the x squared terms will then cancel out and we then have a linear equation

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:38.530
We can routinely solve this equation for x and we get that x is equal to 3 over 4

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.410
Let's substitute that into our diagram

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:45.309
We now want to consider the area of the overlapping region

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.029
Let's also consider the area of this right triangle, which is congruent to the other right triangle

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:57.879
We thus have the area of this overlapping region plus the area of two of these

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:01.029
triangles will be equal to the area of the original rectangle

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:05.769
The rectangle has an area equal to 2 times 1 which is equal to 2

00:02:06.349 --> 00:02:12.849
two of these triangles will have an area equal to 3 over 4 multiplied by 1 which is equal to 3 over 4

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.599
We thus can solve for the area of the overlapping region and it will be equal to 2 minus 3 over 4

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.169
Which is equal to 5 over 4, and that's our answer

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:29.460
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.740
As always thanks for watching and thanks for your support

